# Playwright Quick Reference

*A short cheat sheet to skim anytime — not a full tutorial.*

---

## 1. Setup & Run
```bash
npm init playwright@latest      # create project
npx playwright test             # run all tests
npx playwright test --ui        # run in UI mode (great for debugging)
npx playwright test --headed    # see the browser while running
npx playwright codegen <url>    # auto-generate test code by clicking around
```

## 2. Basic Test Structure
```js
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('login test', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('https://example.com');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('test@test.com');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Login' }).click();
  await expect(page.getByText('Welcome')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## 3. Locators (preferred → least preferred)
```js
page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' })   // best - accessible
page.getByLabel('Username')
page.getByPlaceholder('Enter email')
page.getByText('Sign up')
page.getByTestId('submit-btn')                 // needs data-testid in HTML
page.locator('css=.class-name')                // fallback only
```

## 4. Common Actions
```js
await page.click(selector)
await page.fill(selector, 'text')
await page.type(selector, 'text')      // simulates typing
await page.check(selector)             // checkbox/radio
await page.selectOption(selector, 'value')
await page.hover(selector)
await page.press(selector, 'Enter')
```

## 5. Assertions
```js
await expect(locator).toBeVisible()
await expect(locator).toHaveText('text')
await expect(locator).toHaveValue('text')
await expect(locator).toBeEnabled()
await expect(locator).toBeChecked()
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/)
await expect(page).toHaveTitle('My App')
```

## 6. Waits (Playwright auto-waits — you rarely need manual waits)
```js
await page.waitForSelector(selector)
await page.waitForURL('**/dashboard')
await page.waitForLoadState('networkidle')
```
👉 Avoid `page.waitForTimeout()` unless absolutely necessary — it's a fixed delay, not a smart wait.

## 7. Handling Common Situations
```js
// New tab / popup
const [newPage] = await Promise.all([
  context.waitForEvent('page'),
  page.click('a[target="_blank"]'),
]);

// iframe
const frame = page.frameLocator('#iframe-id');
await frame.getByRole('button').click();

// Alert/dialog
page.on('dialog', dialog => dialog.accept());
```

## 8. Page Object Model (POM) — basic shape
```js
// pages/LoginPage.js
export class LoginPage {
  constructor(page) {
    this.page = page;
    this.emailInput = page.getByLabel('Email');
    this.loginBtn = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Login' });
  }
  async login(email, password) {
    await this.emailInput.fill(email);
    await this.page.getByLabel('Password').fill(password);
    await this.loginBtn.click();
  }
}

// in test file
const loginPage = new LoginPage(page);
await loginPage.login('a@a.com', 'pass123');
```
**Why:** keeps locators/actions in one place → easier to maintain when UI changes.

## 9. API Testing in Playwright
```js
const response = await request.get('https://api.site.com/users');
expect(response.status()).toBe(200);
const body = await response.json();
expect(body.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```

## 10. Debugging
```bash
npx playwright test --debug     # step through test
npx playwright show-report      # view HTML report after a run
```

